ntdll: arm64ec: stop stack walks that leave the real frames

Arknights: Endfield hung at its logo: its main thread spent all its time in
RtlWalkFrameChain, which Unity's IL2CPP calls (through RtlCaptureStackBackTrace) to record a
stack trace while the game starts. Two things in the ARM64EC ntdll made such a walk derail:

- RtlWalkFrameChain carried on when RtlLookupFunctionEntry found no unwind data. The unwind
  then treats the code as a leaf and takes the word at the stack pointer as the return
  address, which in the middle of an emulated x64 frame is not one, and the walk slides up the
  stack through whatever it finds. The x86_64 version stops there (`if (!func) break;`); so
  does this one now.
- RtlIsEcCode looked every address up in the EC code bitmap without checking it is inside it.
  A walk that has left the real frames asks about junk (0x41006c0060xxxx, which is UTF-16
  text, was seen), the read faults, and the fault's own dispatch walks the same stack and
  faults again. Addresses above user memory are now simply not EC code.

These are the two fixes FineWine Patcher applies to CrossOver ARM's ntdll.dll as binary edits
(ArmNtdllFix), which made Endfield get past its logo and into the world there.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
@@ -1397,6 +1397,11 @@
 {
     const UINT64 *map = (const UINT64 *)NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->EcCodeBitMap;
     ULONG_PTR page = ptr / page_size;
+    /* FineWine: the map has one bit per page of user memory and no more. Stack walks and
+     * unwinds ask about whatever is in a return-address slot, junk included (a walk that
+     * left the real frames was seen asking about 0x41006c0060xxxx, UTF-16 text); reading the
+     * map that far out faulted, and the fault was unwound in turn, over and over. */
+    if (ptr >= 0x800000000000) return FALSE;
     return (map[page / 64] >> (page & 63)) & 1;
 }
 
@@ -1854,6 +1859,12 @@
         pc = context.Rip;
         if ((context.ContextFlags & CONTEXT_UNWOUND_TO_CALL) && RtlIsEcCode( pc )) pc -= 4;
         func = RtlLookupFunctionEntry( pc, &base, &table );
+        /* FineWine: as the x86_64 walk does. Without unwind data the unwind treats the code as
+         * a leaf and takes the return address from the top of the stack, which in the middle
+         * of an emulated x64 frame is not one; the walk then wanders up the stack through
+         * whatever it finds. Unity's IL2CPP captures stack traces this way (Arknights:
+         * Endfield's GameAssembly does at start-up), and the game hung at its logo. */
+        if (!func) break;
         if (RtlVirtualUnwind2( UNW_FLAG_NHANDLER, base, pc, func, &context, NULL,
                                &data, &frame, NULL, NULL, NULL, &handler, 0 ))
             break;
